## Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card which flips (rotates) around the Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Container that gives the 3D perspective */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* How far the viewer is from the card */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* 2️⃣  The card itself – a 3D element */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;  /* Keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s;    /* Smooth animation */
}

/* 3️⃣  Flip the card on hover */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);    /* Rotate 180° around Y‑axis */
}

/* 4️⃣  Front & Back faces */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;  /* Hide the back face when it's turned away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #fff;
}

/* Front face */
.card-front {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4e54c8, #8f94fb);
}

/* Back face – rotate it 180° so it starts hidden */
.card-back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff416c, #ff4b2b);
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      <p>Front side</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      <p>Back side</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | CSS property |
|------|--------------|--------------|
| 1 | The wrapper gives the 3D space (`perspective`) | `perspective: 1000px;` |
| 2 | The card keeps its children in 3D (`transform-style`) | `transform-style: preserve-3d;` |
| 3 | On hover we rotate the card 180° around the Y‑axis | `transform: rotateY(180deg);` |
| 4 | Each face is absolutely positioned, covers the whole card, and hides its back side when turned away | `backface-visibility: hidden;` |

You can replace the gradients, text, or add images inside the faces to suit your design.  
Happy coding!
